  note={ICRA 2025},
  abstract={Inspired by the neural structure of the stick insect Carausius morosus, we introduce the Distributed Neural Locomotion Controller (D-NLC), a modular control framework that uses local proprioceptive feedback to modulate joint-level Central Pattern Generator signals and produce emergent locomotive behaviors. Implemented on a modular legged robot with distributed joint-level embedded computing, D-NLC achieves a 31.3% average increase in curvilinear motion performance under terrain and amputation perturbations compared to a centralized predefined gait controller, without numerical optimization or weight training.},
